= Database — Simple =

A '''database''' is an organized collection of data meant to be stored and used over time.

A database management system, or DBMS, is the software that manages the database.

They are not the same thing.

Databases can organize information as tables, documents, key–value records, graphs, or other structures.

A database can support searching, updating, rules about valid data, permissions, backups, and transactions.

SQL is commonly used with relational databases.

